# The image is built by `COPY . .` and then `go build ./cmd/ghchronicle`, so
# everything this file does not name is uploaded to the daemon on every build,
# and every change to any of it invalidates the cached compile. What the build
# actually reads is go.mod, go.sum, version.go with the VERSION file it embeds,
# cmd/ and internal/, about one megabyte. The context measured 542 MB before the
# entries below existed.
#
# Deliberately a denylist. An allowlist would be tighter, but it silently drops
# whatever is added at the root later that the build does need, and the build
# does read the root.
#
# Stricter than gitlab-mcp-server's .dockerignore on purpose, and the owner's
# decision, to be kept when the two are aligned again. Beyond what that file
# excludes, this one keeps out config.yaml and *.token, so a local
# configuration or GitHub token never reaches a layer of an image, and site/,
# the host's own binaries and the scanner's working directory, so the context
# stays near the megabyte the build reads instead of hundreds of them.

# Working notes: not part of the published tool.
plan/

# History and CI definitions: the build reads neither, and .git alone is the
# second largest thing in the tree.
.git
.github

# Local configuration and credentials must never reach an image layer. `.env.*`
# is the variant a second environment gets (.env.local, .env.production), and
# it holds the same kind of secret as the file it copies.
config.yaml
.env
.env.*
*.token

# Build output from the host: bin/ is `make build`, dist/ is `make build-all`
# and GoReleaser, and the loose files are what `go build ./cmd/<name>`, `go
# test`, `make coverage` and `make cover-check` leave in the working directory:
# coverage.out and coverage.html. The eight command
# names are spelled out because none of them carries an extension, and together
# they are 84 MB of host binary that the image build would upload and then
# ignore, since it compiles its own from source. golangci-report*.txt is a lint
# run saved to a file for reading later, which the build has no use for either.
#
# Unlike .gitignore, a pattern here is matched against the whole path, so
# "probe" names the file at the root and cannot reach cmd/probe.
bin/
dist/
check_dashboards
check_postgres
check_prometheus
gen_brand
gen_dashboards
ghchronicle
probe
publish_dashboard
*.exe
*.test
*.out
coverage*
golangci-report*.txt

# The scanner's configuration, and the working directory `make sonar` leaves at
# the root: sonar-project.properties sets no sonar.working.directory, so
# sonar-scanner uses its default. The image build reads neither.
sonar-project.properties
.scannerwork/

# The documentation site: node_modules alone is 598 MB, and nothing in the
# image reads a line of it. This one entry is most of the difference between a
# 542 MB context and the 1.6 MB one it is now.
site/

# Prose, images and generated dashboards. None of it is embedded: the module's
# only go:embed is in version.go, which reads the VERSION file beside it at the
# root, and neither of those two is excluded here. So copying these in would
# only invalidate the compile layer every time a document is edited.
#
# Before excluding anything else at the root, check it is not what version.go
# embeds: a build that cannot see VERSION does not fail, it reports "dev".
docs/
brand/
dashboards/
*.md

# The end-to-end suite builds its own binary and drives it against a fake
# GitHub. The image build never compiles it.
test/
